          "body": "## Summary\n\nHoist the command encoder, pipeline, input/output bindings, and scan-size binding shared by the contiguous and strided Metal scan paths.\n\nThe branch-specific stride bindings and thread-grid calculations remain unchanged. This removes six net production lines without changing scan kernels or dispatch.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Release Metal build and Python bindings with C++20 and warnings as errors\n- Native Metal scan operation test (12/12 assertions)\n- Native Metal scan gradient test (20/20 assertions)\n- Python scan, logcumsumexp, and NaN cummax/cummin tests\n- Baseline-matched full native suite\n- Object-size and global-symbol comparison\n- Fully paginated open-PR overlap and collision scan\n- `clang-format` and `git diff --check`",
